\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The Mac app should only exist if it does something the Chrome extension cannot do cleanly. Otherwise, it is unnecessary complexity.\
Its strongest purpose would be to act as the user's 
\f1\b persistent accessibility profile and local intelligence layer
\f0\b0 . The user opens the Mac app once to define things like text size, visual density, motor limitations, preferred guidance level, contrast, motion sensitivity, and whether the system can adapt automatically. That profile then follows them across every website Chrome visits.\
The second purpose is 
\f1\b local AI processing
\f0\b0 . If you want the system to use a local model to understand page structure, infer what is important, or decide how aggressively to simplify something, the Mac app is a much better place to run that model than inside a Chrome extension. The extension can send a structured page representation to the Mac app, get back adaptation instructions, and then modify the page.\
It could also serve as the user's 
\f1\b control center
\f0\b0 : pause adaptation, see which sites were modified, whitelist/blacklist sites, adjust preferences, reset a site's layout, inspect why something changed, and control privacy/retention.\
But for your senior project, I would make one important distinction:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 You probably do not need the Mac app for version 1.
\f0\b0 \
A Chrome extension alone can store preferences, inspect pages, monitor behavior, and modify the DOM. You could build the entire core idea as:\

\f1\b Chrome extension \uc0\u8594  user profile \u8594  adaptation engine \u8594  modified website
\f0\b0 \
Then add the Mac app only if you need local-model inference or want the finished product to feel like a persistent system-level accessibility product.\
So I would think of it this way:\

\f1\b Chrome extension = hands and eyes.
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 It sees the webpage and changes it.\

\f1\b Mac app = memory and brain.
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 It knows the user and decides how the web should adapt.\
If the \'93brain\'94 is simple enough to live inside the extension, don't force a Mac app into the architecture. The product idea is stronger if every component has a clear reason to exist.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
